                <pb facs="0742" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg728"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish Secretary of
                        State, to Mr. Hoar, Attorney-General.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><seg type="margin">[744]</seg> *<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-05-15"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 15, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a copy of a
                    translation of a note of the — instant, addressed to this Department by Mr.
                    Evariste La Roche, <pb facs="0743" n="729" xml:id="pg729"/> chargé d’affaires of
                    Hayti, setting forth the reasons he still entertains for the opinion that the
                    steamer Florida at Chester, Pennsylvania, has been prepared and is about to
                    start for the purpose of engaging in hostilities against his government. The
                    expediency of requiring the security which Mr. La Roche indicates against a
                    violation of the law of the United States in this case is submitted to your
                    early consideration.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Rockwood Hoar</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Attorney-General.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
